# Bank 12 (runs at 0xA000). Directives: L label, C line comment, B block
# header, D data range, F row width.
#
# THIS BANK HOLDS NO CODE. It is the second half of the MAP: it always goes
# hand in hand with bank 11 (0x8000), which is mapped at the same time, so a
# stage's script can start in one bank and end in the other.

D 0xA000 0xB2E4 scripts_2  The scripts of stages 7 to 12 (0xA098, 0xA2D8, 0xA428, 0xA578 and 0xA668), pointed to by table 0x97DE in bank 11. The stretch from 0xA000 to 0xA097 is the tail of the script that starts at 0x9F18, in bank 11.
F 0xA000 6
D 0xB2E4 0xB2EC endings_table  Four words (0xB2EC, 0xB379, 0xB3F4, 0xB48A). Read by 0x5D95 in bank 0 with `ld hl,0xB2D2` and 0x47AE, that is, with the base declared EIGHT WORDS further back: only indices 9 to 12 are valid, and the entries for stages 1 to 8 would land on top of the previous script. It is the same trick as table 0x42AD.
F 0xB2E4 w2
D 0xB2EC 0xB649 ending_records  What the table above points to: groups of three bytes (a count, and a word) that 0x5DAA reads with `ld c,(hl) / ld e,(hl) / ld d,(hl)`.
F 0xB2EC 3
D 0xB649 0xC000 filler  0xFF filler up to the bank's 8192 bytes.
F 0xB649 16
